|~ What is declared under `::error`, the kind every error is a value
   of: the refusal of an error whose path is no vector of stops, and the
   verbs of errors. The error `!|` opens is `::error{…}`, or the tag of
   the site that refused stacked over it, and its walk passes `::error`
   on its way to the map, so a verb declared here reaches every error. ~|

:error/TrailNotVecError
  |~~ `:trail` on an error descriptor is the path of the error, a
      vector of stops the runtime writes, `{:step :subject :skipped}`,
      from the step where it arose to the step where it is read.
      An error literal or a `raise` that writes a value that is no plain
      vector under `:trail`, a set, a quote and a doc among them, is
      refused as it makes the error. A `raise`
      that writes the `:trail` it read goes on with that path, and one
      that leaves it out starts a path at its own step.
      ::link~(::error | doc)
  ~~|

:error/TrailNotVecError/refusesANumberForATrail
  |~~ A number given as a trail is refused. ~~|
  ::law~(!{:kind :oops :trail 5} !| [type /actualType] | eq [::error/TrailNotVecError ::number])

:error/TrailNotVecError/refusesATrailLaidOverAnError
  |~~ A trail of a number laid over an error is refused when it is raised. ~~|
  ::law~(!{:kind :oops} | count !| union {:trail 5} | raise !| type | eq ::error/TrailNotVecError)

:error/TrailNotVecError/startsATrailAtTheRaise
  |~~ An error raised without a trail starts its trail at the raise. ~~|
  ::law~(!{:kind :oops} | count !| minus #[:trail] | raise | add 1 !| /trail * /step | eq [~(raise)])

:error/index
  |~~ The place of the element refused, counted from zero. ~~|
  ::number

:error/actualType
  |~~ The kind of the value refused. ~~|
  ::tag

:error/places
  |~~ How many places the parts of the word read, where the call gave
      more values.
  ~~|
  ::number

:error/actualValue
  |~~ The value refused, where it is not the subject that the first stop
      of the trail holds.
  ~~|
  ::any

:error/trail
  |~~ The path of the error: each step it passed, from the one
      that raised it, with the subject that step met and the steps
      skipped after it.
  ~~|
  ~(/trail)

:error/trail/holdsTheStepThatRaised
  |~~ The trail of an error raised at once holds the one step. ~~|
  ::law~("x" | add 1 !| trail | count | eq 1)

:error/trail/namesTheStepsSkipped
  |~~ The stop of the step that raised names the steps skipped after it. ~~|
  ::law~("x" | add 1 | mul 2 !| trail | first | /skipped | eq ~(mul 2))

:error/trail/stops
  |~~ The stops of the path the error took. ~~|
  ::vec
